---
import DocsLayout from '../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro';
---

<DocsLayout title="Directives — IonPath" current="/guides/directives/">
  <div class="animate-fade-in-up">
    <h1 class="text-3xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-2">Directives</h1>
    <p class="text-text-secondary mb-8">Directives are file-level instructions that control imports and feature flags. They appear at the top of <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">.ion</code> files before any type declarations.</p>
  </div>

  <div class="space-y-12 animate-fade-in-up-delay-1">

    <section>
      <h2 id="import" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">#import — Import Types</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">Import specific types from another module or file:</p>
      <div class="code-block text-[13px]">
        <pre><span class="text-accent-3">#import</span> {'{'} <span class="type-name">User</span>, <span class="type-name">Role</span> {'}'} <span class="type-keyword">from</span> <span class="text-accent-2">"auth"</span>
<span class="text-accent-3">#import</span> {'{'} <span class="type-name">OrderItem</span> {'}'} <span class="text-accent-2">from</span> <span class="text-accent-2">"shop"</span>

<span class="text-accent-3">service</span> <span class="type-name">UserService</span>() {'{'}
    GetUser(id: <span class="type-keyword">u4</span>): <span class="type-name">User</span>;  <span class="text-text-muted">// User is imported from "auth" module</span>
{'}'}</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-3">Module names reference external modules declared in <a href="/guides/ion-config/" class="text-accent hover:underline">ion.config.json</a>. Only the listed types become available in the current scope. See <a href="/guides/modules/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Modules</a> for more details on how the module system works.</p>

      <div class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-status-down/20 bg-status-down-subtle p-4">
        <span class="text-status-down text-sm mt-0.5">✕</span>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary"><strong>Circular imports are forbidden.</strong> If module A imports from B and B imports from A, the compiler reports <a href="/guides/diagnostics/#ION0040" class="text-accent hover:underline">ION0040</a>.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="use" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">#use — Import File (Deprecated)</h2>
      <div class="flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-status-degraded/20 bg-status-degraded-subtle p-4 mb-4">
        <span class="text-status-degraded text-sm mt-0.5">⚠</span>
        <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary"><strong>Deprecated.</strong> The <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">#use</code> directive is deprecated (<a href="/guides/diagnostics/#ION0047" class="text-accent hover:underline">ION0047</a>). Use <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">#import {'{'} Type {'}'} from "module"</code> instead.</p>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">Legacy syntax for importing all types from a local file:</p>
      <div class="code-block text-[13px]">
        <pre><span class="text-accent-3">#use</span> <span class="text-accent-2">"common.ion"</span>
<span class="text-accent-3">#use</span> <span class="text-accent-2">"models/user.ion"</span></pre>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-3">Paths are relative to the current file's directory. All type declarations from the imported file become available in the current scope.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="feature" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">#feature — Declare a Required Feature</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4"><code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">#feature</code> declares that <strong>this file requires</strong> the named feature. It does not switch a feature on — features are enabled for the whole project, in the <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">features</code> array of <a href="/guides/ion-config/" class="text-accent hover:underline">ion.config.json</a>. The directive is an assertion the compiler checks: if the project does not enable the feature, compilation fails with <a href="/guides/diagnostics/#ION0049" class="text-accent hover:underline">ION0049</a>, naming the config key you need to add and listing what is currently enabled. A feature name the compiler does not know at all is also ION0049 — the set is closed, so "add it to the config" would be bad advice.</p>
      <div class="code-block text-[13px]">
        <pre><span class="text-accent-3">#feature</span> <span class="text-accent-2">"orleans"</span>

<span class="text-accent-3">service</span> <span class="type-name">GrainService</span>() {'{'}
    Ping(): <span class="type-keyword">void</span>;
{'}'}</pre>
      </div>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-3">The directive takes one double-quoted string and no semicolon. A file may declare more than one.</p>

      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-4 mb-2">The features a project may enable:</p>
      <div class="type-grid mt-2">
        <div class="type-grid-header">
          <span>Feature</span>
          <span>Provides</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-keyword">std</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">All primitive types, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Maybe&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Array&lt;T&gt;</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Partial&lt;T&gt;</code>, standard attributes</span>
        </div>
        <div class="type-grid-row">
          <span class="font-mono text-[12px] type-keyword">orleans</span>
          <span class="text-[12px] text-text-secondary">Microsoft Orleans grain-aware code generation</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-accent/20 bg-accent-subtle p-4">
        <span class="text-accent text-sm mt-0.5">i</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium mb-1">What this directive used to do: nothing</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary"><code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">#feature</code> parsed into the syntax tree and was read by no part of the compiler. It could name a feature that did not exist, or contradict the project configuration, and the build succeeded either way — the only consumer was the editor's syntax highlighter. It is checked now.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="mt-4 flex items-start gap-3 rounded-xl border border-status-degraded/20 bg-status-degraded-subtle p-4">
        <span class="text-status-degraded text-sm mt-0.5">⚠</span>
        <div>
          <p class="text-sm font-medium mb-1">The <code class="font-mono text-[12px]">vector</code> feature has been removed</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary">A third feature, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">vector</code>, used to exist. It declared nine builtin types — <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">vec2f</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">vec3f</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">vec4f</code> and the same in <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">d</code> and <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">h</code> precisions — intended for vector maths. It has been deleted as unimplemented: the names resolved in the compiler and the language server, but <strong>no generator mapped them to anything</strong> and <strong>no runtime defined them</strong>, so every target fell through to emitting the raw Ion name and enabling the feature produced output that did not compile in any language. Vector types may return later as a well-known-type feature with real runtime support; the names above are free until then.</p>
          <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mt-2">This page previously described the feature as providing <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Vector2</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Vector3</code>, <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Vector4</code> and <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">Quaternion</code>. Those four names never existed in Ion at all, even while the feature did — they were the C# types the language server's hover text claimed the <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">vec*</code> names mapped to, and no generator ever emitted them either.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2 id="module-system" class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Module System</h2>
      <p class="text-sm text-text-secondary mb-4">Each <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1.5 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">.ion</code> file is a module. The compiler processes all <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">.ion</code> files in the project directory and resolves imports across files. For external module dependencies, see the <a href="/guides/modules/" class="text-accent hover:underline">Modules</a> guide.</p>
      <ol class="list-decimal list-inside space-y-2 text-sm text-text-secondary">
        <li>Parse all <code class="bg-oled-elevated px-1 py-0.5 rounded font-mono text-[11px]">.ion</code> files</li>
        <li>Resolve external module dependencies from <a href="/guides/ion-config/" class="text-accent hover:underline">ion.config.json</a></li>
        <li>Detect import cycles (<a href="/guides/diagnostics/#ION0001" class="text-accent hover:underline">ION0001</a>, <a href="/guides/diagnostics/#ION0040" class="text-accent hover:underline">ION0040</a>)</li>
        <li>Resolve type references across modules</li>
        <li>Validate and generate code</li>
      </ol>
    </section>

  </div>
</DocsLayout>
